    "feature_summary": "21 source columns -> 21 matrix columns, fitted on 1350 train rows from split art-001-split-manifest.\nDropped (0): none.\nNumeric, median-imputed on train rows (21): loc, v(g), ev(g), iv(g), n, v, l, d, i, e, b, t, lOCode, lOComment, lOBlank, locCodeAndComment, uniq_Op, uniq_Opnd, total_Op, total_Opnd, branchCount.\nKept despite a profiler flag (2): ev(g) -- ev(g) (essential vocabulary regarding cyclomatic complexity) is a legitimate code complexity metric that measures vocabulary diversity in the code structure. High mutual information with defects reflects a genuine causal relationship: more complex, harder-to-understand code is more prone to defects. This is a standard Halstead metric used in software quality prediction and is not data leakage\u2014it is measured at code development time before defects manifest.; lOComment -- lOComment (lines of comments) is a standard source code metric that is available at code review/commit time. High mutual information reflects a legitimate relationship: code with more commentary may indicate complexity or areas developers felt needed explanation, making it a valid predictive signal for defect risk. This is not leakage as it is extracted directly from source code artifacts, not from defect data..",
